;; giemon-factory-r0 — 建築手順 (construction procedure / 4D施工シーケンス),
;; Datomic-style EDN. SSoT for the ORDER in which the plant is built — full MEP +
;; 外構, with each step assigned a 施工ロボット (:step/robot → robots.edn).
;;
;; The plant is designed to be BUILT by robotics (tatekata 建方, ADR-2605250715).
;; `kotoba_gen.py` emits:
;;   - one kotoba entity per step → kg/claim/step/* datoms (EAVT, ADR-2605312345),
;;     with :step/depends-on / :step/consumes as ENTITY-REF claims, plus
;;     :step/robot linking the assigned construction robot, and
;;   - construction.order.json → consumed by kami-app-giemon-factory (geometry
;;     reveal) and kami-app-tatekata (the assigned robot builds each step on
;;     kami-genesis; concrete/steel steps drive a material-process field).
;;
;; :step/robot       施工ロボット id (robots.edn :robot/registry)
;; :step/depends-on  vector of prior :step/id (predecessors → entity refs)
;; :step/consumes    vector of :part/id from building.edn (materials drawn)
;; :step/reveals     vector of render element ids in factory.scene.json
;; :step/duration-d  nominal duration in working days (schedule)
;; :step/trade       responsible trade / 工種

{:proc/meta
 {:proc/of        "giemon-factory-r0"
  :proc/revision  "v3"
  :proc/title     "Giemon robot plant — R0 construction sequence (4D, full MEP + 外構 + 施工ロボット)"
  :proc/method    "robotic design-build, single 80x50m bay, steel portal frame + 構内外構"
  :proc/note      "R0 design sequence. depends-on encodes hard logic; :step/robot assigns the construction robot per trade (robots.edn). Durations are nominal; the buildability check estimates robot cycle-time vs these."}

 :proc/steps
